Harlan, I looked at the storefront head condition at the north arcade on Th=
ursday as you asked. The problem is at the receptor, where the thermal brea=
k in the head member stops short of the interior face and the aluminum rece=
ptor bridges straight through to the framing.<br />
<br />
I ran the interior surface temperature against the design interior conditio=
ns and the head runs about four degrees below dew point on a design winter =
night with the retail humidification the tenants are asking for. That will =
drip. Closing the gap with a low expansion foam and a continuous interior s=
ealant bead moves it back above dew point, and it is a cheap fix if it happ=
ens before the ceilings close.